  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Far and near – two shots on the goalkeeper",
  "description": "Half the court, goalkeeper in goal. The shooters' line A with balls stands by the boards level with the centre line, feeder B by the opposite boards across from them, and feeder C with balls along the same boards as A, a little closer to goal. A plays a cross pass to B and sets off towards goal. B plays the ball into A's run, and A takes a first shot from distance. A carries straight on towards goal, gets a pass from C and shoots again close in.\n\nThe focus is on the goalkeeper: save the first shot, get up and set for the new angle before the next one. Rotate: A becomes B, B becomes C and C joins the A line. Switch sides after a few minutes.\n\nVariant: C plays the second pass hard across the front of goal and A only deflects it in. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: after the first save – up quickly and find your position again."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: follow C's pass with your eyes and move to the new angle before the shot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A: do not stop after the first shot, carry straight on to the next finishing spot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Feeders: pass into A's path so the shots come at speed."
    }
  ],
